{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Opened the one route the verify question's gap still left open as a child question (@stall_route) and requested its execution. The source analysis says the stale-read consequence needs a successor elected while the old leader still reports verify success, and the leader's lease case becomes ready no later than LeaderLeaseTimeout, so the remaining legal route is a leader whose own main loop is blocked past that point. The probe models it with a wrapping log store whose StoreLogs blocks the caller — the leader's main loop — while a client Apply is in flight, partitions the leader so only the non-voter stays reachable, and queues VerifyLeader during the stall; eight fresh-cluster trials report the verify endpoint, a 1ms leadership sampler over all four servers, the term reached and the stall counters, with two event types so the setup can serve as the comparison admission. Predictions recorded: a successor should be observed in Leader state while the stalled leader is still Leader, and whether any queued verify reports success is exactly what the receipt will decide. No observation is claimed yet; a local compilation and construction run was used only to check the harness, and the formal clean-copy receipt is pending.\"}"}}
